# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
config RUST_TASK_WORK
	bool "Rust task-work queueing, cancellation and execution"
	depends on RUST && X86_64
	default y
	help
	  Build task_work_add(), the cancellation entry points and
	  task_work_run() from kernel/task_work.rs in the original
	  kernel/task_work.o slot. task_work_primitives.o keeps the native
	  field accessors, locks, per-CPU NMI irq_work storage, the
	  callback-bearing public shells and the x86 warning-site expansion.
	  Only the x86-64 warning profile is implemented by that companion.
	  Turning this option off selects the unchanged original C provider.
